    "font" : "Arial-BoldMT",
    "font size" : 9.0,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Fig. 8. Stabilization diagram of the impact testing on the shaker."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 89,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 307.667, 162.223, 540.667, 235.223 ],
    "font" : "TimesNewRomanPSMT",
    "font size" : 9.96,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "When looking at these values, we may observe that the experimental values match the calculated ones for the body-related parameters, especially for the modal mass and the modal stiffness, respectively m 2 and k 2 , and in a less manner for the modal damping c 2 . On the contrary, we have no match for the table-related parameters."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 95,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 307.333, 66.557, 540.667, 161.223 ],
    "font" : "TimesNewRomanPSMT",
    "font size" : 9.96,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "This difference is also noticeable in Figure 8. The response curves of the body (P2-P5) clearly show a resonance, making the body-related parameters identification possible, while the table resonance, identified in the stabilization diagram to be located at 69,104Hz, is not visible (P1). We may conclude that the experimentally determined table-related parameters are not valid."
  } ]
